{"name":"Raindrop","hex":"#9ec6c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raindrop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single droplet of rainwater that has just fallen or is falling from the sky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raindrop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drop (liquid)","blocks":[{"text":"A drop or droplet is a small column of liquid, bounded completely or almost completely by free surfaces. A drop may form when liquid accumulates at the end of a tube or other surface boundary, producing a hanging drop called a pendant drop. Drops may also be formed by the condensation of a vapor or by atomization of a larger mass of solid. Water vapor will condense into droplets depending on the temperature. The temperature at which droplets form is called the dew point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Water_drop_light_art_vijayanrajapuram_01.jpg/330px-Water_drop_light_art_vijayanrajapuram_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drop_(liquid)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Water_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Water_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A water drop falling from a tap","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif/120px-Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","s